    "tiptap_body": {
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Hi ",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "Hi "
              },
              {
                "type": "mention",
                "attrs": {
                  "sgid": "BAh7CEkiCGdpZAY6BkVUSSI8Z2lkOi8vanVtcHN0YXJ0LWFwcC9Db21tdW5pdHlNZW1iZXIvNzUzNDk3MDc_ZXhwaXJlc19pbgY7AFRJIgxwdXJwb3NlBjsAVEkiFHJpY2hfdGV4dF9maWVsZAY7AFRJIg9leHBpcmVzX2F0BjsAVDA=--f50aa46255391afdc7b0c54f282646fcee243174"
                },
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "@Yujin Lee"
              },
              {
                "text": " Hi Yujin,",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": " Hi Yujin,"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "I believe the recommendation is to focus on one core process now to avoid becoming overwhelmed. However, in the long run, if you have distinct customer journeys for each service, creating a core process for each product line may make sense. Have you considered grouping the one-off and retainer services? They might share enough similarities to be categorized as two core service types that encompass all your offerings.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "I believe the recommendation is to focus on one core process now to avoid becoming overwhelmed. However, in the long run, if you have distinct customer journeys for each service, creating a core process for each product line may make sense. Have you considered grouping the one-off and retainer services? They might share enough similarities to be categorized as two core service types that encompass all your offerings."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Although the services we provide are very different, I related to your point about having both retainer and one-off clients. My commercial landscaping business engages with customers similarly as our work falls into two primary models: (1) recurring monthly maintenance contracts (similar to your retainer clients) and (2) one-off enhancement or project-based services (similar to your one-off clients).  ",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "Although the services we provide are very different, I related to your point about having both retainer and one-off clients. My commercial landscaping business engages with customers similarly as our work falls into two primary models: (1) recurring monthly maintenance contracts (similar to your retainer clients) and (2) one-off enhancement or project-based services (similar to your one-off clients).  "
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "For this cohort I’m focusing on just one core process: recurring maintenance contracts.  Although we offer many types of enhancement or project-based work, we consider the customer journey similar enough to group into one core process. Therefore, even though we offer many different services, we will limit our core processes to just two.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "For this cohort I’m focusing on just one core process: recurring maintenance contracts.  Although we offer many types of enhancement or project-based work, we consider the customer journey similar enough to group into one core process. Therefore, even though we offer many different services, we will limit our core processes to just two."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "circle_ios_fallback_text": "Hi @Yujin Lee Hi Yujin,I believe the recommendation is to focus on one core process now to avoid becoming overwhelmed. However, in the long run, if you have distinct customer journeys for each service, creating a core process for each product line may make sense. Have you considered grouping the one-off and retainer services? They might share enough similarities to be categorized as two core service types that encompass all your offerings.Although the services we provide are very different, I related to your point about having both retainer and one-off clients. My commercial landscaping business engages with customers similarly as our work falls into two primary models: (1) recurring monthly maintenance contracts (similar to your retainer clients) and (2) one-off enhancement or project-based services (similar to your one-off clients).  For this cohort I’m focusing on just one core process: recurring maintenance contracts.  Although we offer many types of enhancement or project-based work, we consider the customer journey similar enough to group into one core process. Therefore, even though we offer many different services, we will limit our core processes to just two.",
